From 4598b5f4fda04c40e64faebd979eb1037b275ef6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jacob Oursland <jacob.oursland@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 7 Sep 2026 17:26:50 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] MT: stop losing updates on the factor's entry counters

FrontMtx_storeFront() accumulates frontmtx->nentD, nentL and nentU with
plain read-modify-writes at ten sites, and every factorization thread
runs it concurrently for the fronts it owns.  ThreadSanitizer reported
three of these directly.

The counters feed the operation-count and storage statistics only --
FrontMtx_nentD()/nentL()/nentU() and the driver's nops estimate -- so
the damage is an understated report, not a wrong answer.  They are
still a lost-update race and still undefined behaviour, and they are
the last thing standing between the factorization and a clean
ThreadSanitizer run, so make them relaxed atomic fetch-adds.  Relaxed
is sufficient: nothing is published through these counters, and no
ordering is required, so the cost is a single LDADD on aarch64 and
LOCK XADD on x86, ten times per front.
---
 FrontMtx/src/storeFront.c | 21 +++++++++++----------
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 10 deletions(-)

diff --git a/FrontMtx/src/storeFront.c b/FrontMtx/src/storeFront.c
index 2465a40..0925d6e 100644
